图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DSH 插件市场：搜索 GitHub dsh-plugin 话题插件，一键安装到本地 dsh（agent 工具 + 设置页插件市场 tab）","id":"gh:1335098475","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-plugin-mall","slug":"1e0zj/dsh-plugin-mall","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","plugin-marketplace"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DSH 插件市场：搜索 GitHub dsh-plugin 话题插件，一键安装到本地 dsh（agent 工具 + 设置页插件市场 tab）"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-plugin-mall"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**An open plugin marketplace for DeepSeek Harness (dsh): search every GitHub repo tagged `topic:dsh-"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"plugin`, automatically verify which ones are real dsh plugins, install and update with one click.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"中文说明 · Install · Why another marketplace · Roadmap"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Two surfaces: a **Settings → Plugins → Marketplace** tab in the dsh web UI, and five agent tools usa"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ble from any session."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Why another marketplace?"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Curated lists only show what has been reviewed and merged. This marketplace is open by construction:"},{"id":"p7s2","text":" **any repo tagged `topic:dsh-plugin` is discoverable the moment it is pushed** — no submission, no "},{"id":"p7s3","text":"approval queue. To keep that openness usable:"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- **Automatic verification** — every search result's `package.json` is fetched (jsDelivr/raw dual-so"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"urce CDN, no API quota) and checked for the official `dsh.bundle` / `dsh.client` manifest. Verified "},{"id":"p8s3","text":"plugins get a green badge; the default \"verified only\" view filters out ~73% of topic noise (empty r"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"epos and unrelated projects riding the tag).\n- **Browse-time compatibility badges** — each card is a"},{"id":"p8s5","text":"lso statically scanned against your profile before you click anything: declared conflicts, exclusive"},{"id":"p8s6","text":" groups, loader-id collisions (from the repo's patch file), rows the candidate's patch would switch "},{"id":"p8s7","text":"off or reconfigure in the profile you already run, host-module shadowing, and peer/Node/OS ranges. C"},{"id":"p8s8","text":"ards show 适配 / 有风险 / 冲突 / 适配未知 accordingly — advisory only; the install preflight remains the enforc"},{"id":"p8s9","text":"ing gate.\n- **Anti-squatting** — an install prefers the npm tarball only when the registry entry's `"},{"id":"p8s10","text":"repository` URL points back to the same GitHub repo; anything else falls back to the explicit `githu"},{"id":"p8s11","text":"b:` spec.\n- **npm-first installs** — registry tarballs are smaller than whole-repo GitHub downloads "},{"id":"p8s12","text":"and come with integrity checks. Lookups follow the registry pnpm actually installs from (profile `.n"},{"id":"p8s13","text":"pmrc` → `pnpm config get registry` → npmjs), so a mirror user keeps npm-first instead of silently fa"},{"id":"p8s14","text":"lling back to whole-repo clones.\n- **Update management** — installed plugins are compared against th"},{"id":"p8s15","text":"e registry `latest`; one-click update per plugin.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Restart dsh after installing."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"> **`link:` cannot be set up right now**, for reasons upstream of this plugin. Under\n> `link:` Node "},{"id":"p12s2","text":"loads from the project's real path, so bare imports must resolve from\n> the project's own `node_modu"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"les` — which requires `npm install` inside the project\n> first. That fails: the framework packages' "},{"id":"p12s4","text":"registry dist-tags currently straddle two\n> release trains (`dsh-tools` latest is still `0.0.1-rc.x`"},{"id":"p12s5","text":" while `dsh-app-boot` is on\n> `0.1.0-rc.x`), their peer ranges do not intersect, and npm stops with "},{"id":"p12s6","text":"ERESOLVE.\n> Neither escape hatch helps — `--legacy-peer-deps` skips peers so bare imports still\n> wi"},{"id":"p12s7","text":"ll not resolve, and `--force` plants a mixed-train copy of the framework inside the\n> project, which"},{"id":"p12s8","text":" `link:` would then load instead of the host's, causing exactly the\n> duplicate-module crash describ"},{"id":"p12s9","text":"ed under 开发说明. Until those dist-tags line up,\n> develop against a local tarball — `npm pack`, then i"},{"id":"p12s10","text":"nstall the `.tgz` with a `file:`\n> spec (recipe in the 安装 section below). Do not hand-overwrite file"},{"id":"p12s11","text":"s under\n> `node_modules`: they are hard-linked into pnpm's global store, and any later\n> `pnpm add/r"},{"id":"p12s12","text":"emove` rebuilds the tree and restores them anyway.\n>\n> Re-packing and running `add` again does **not"},{"id":"p12s13","text":"hing**: the `file:` spec and the\n> version are unchanged, so pnpm calls it already installed and nev"},{"id":"p12s14","text":"er compares\n> the tarball's bytes. The command succeeds, `package.json` looks right, and\n> `node_mod"},{"id":"p12s15","text":"ules` still holds the previous build. Always `remove` before `add`,\n> or give the test build its own"},{"id":"p12s16","text":" version. Then restart dsh completely — the\n> install ran inside the host process still executing th"},{"id":"p12s17","text":"hen restart dsh completely — the\n> install ran inside the host process still executing the old code."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Startup protection (guard CLI)"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"> **Known issue — every version since v0.3.4, including v0.4.17 (#24):** a plain `dsh web` start may"},{"id":"p14s2","text":" commit and delete the pending snapshot as soon as the marketplace plugin loads, before later loader"},{"id":"p14s3","text":" entries have finished loading. Downgrading is not a workaround — you would have to go back before v"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"0.3.4 and give up every fix since. If a later entry fails, automatic rollback is no longer available"},{"id":"p14s5","text":". Until #24 is fixed, use `guard launch` for the first restart after every marketplace install or up"},{"id":"p14s6","text":"date. The marketplace's **\"Restart dsh\" button already uses the guarded restart path** (it spawns `g"},{"id":"p14s7","text":"uard launch --await-exit`), so restarting from the UI is safe.\n>\n> If the log already shows `startup"},{"id":"p14s8","text":" recovery: committed` and the start then fails, `guard recover` usually has no snapshot left to rest"},{"id":"p14s9","text":"ore — repair `cordis.patch.yml` by hand, or restore a profile backup."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"The last line of defense is at **startup**. The package ships a standalone, host-independent CLI (bi"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"n `dsh-plugin-guard`, also runnable by path):"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The bare `dsh-plugin-guard` bin resolves only when the profile's (or global) `.bin` is on `PATH`. Tw"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"o PATH-independent forms:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"**A plain `dsh web` already resolves pending installs.** The marketplace plugin runs\nrecovery when i"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"t loads, so the pending marker is committed — or rolled back, either\nbecause the profile fails valid"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"ation or because the install was left paused at the\nbuild-script approval gate (an unapproved instal"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"l is never committed, however healthy\nit looks). Without this a single install would wedge the profi"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"le — every later install\nand uninstall refuses while a marker is outstanding."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"**What a plain start actually proves is narrower than it looks:** reaching the\nmarketplace's own `ap"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ply` only means the loader got *as far as the position the\nmarketplace occupies* — it does not mean "},{"id":"p20s3","text":"the whole plugin tree composed. Entries\nafter it may still fail to import or apply, and by then the "},{"id":"p20s4","text":"snapshot is already\ngone (that is #24)."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"**`guard launch` is still strictly better**, and for two reasons rather than one:\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## dsh won't start after an update? (affects 0.2.0 – 0.3.2, fixed in 0.3.3)"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Symptom: `dsh web` exits with `cannot resolve profile bundle \"<package>\"`."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Cause: **updating an already-installed plugin** into a rollback (most often the\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
